Re: [perl #47107] English.pm namespace pollution bug Dave Mitchell wrote:
>> blead has the same problem.  Patch is attached.  The solution was to simply
>> only export the scalar values, not the whole glob.  @ARG gave trouble, it's
>> value wasn't being retained when exported as @ARG rather than *ARG.  I suspect
>> @_ magic.  So ARG() will continue to be clobbered.
> 
> It aliases the whole glob for a reason: so that local(), and aliasing
> mechanisms such as for, preserve the mapping between short and long variable
> names.
> 
> if you alias just the glob's scalar slot, it goes wrong:

I didn't know that.  But I didn't do it that way.  The full glob is aliased,
but only the scalar is exported.

However, I see that breaks localization, too... sometimes.  It's weird.
$WARNING and $^W still work but things like $FORMAT_NAME and $LIST_SEPARATOR
don't.

Anyhow, the patch should be reversed.  In its place, put this new test for the
localization.

--- lib/English.t       (/vendor/bleadperl)     (revision 40850)
+++ lib/English.t       (/local/bleadperl)      (revision 40850)
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
     @INC = '../lib';
 }

-use Test::More tests => 55;
+use Test::More tests => 57;

 use English qw( -no_match_vars ) ;
 use Config;
@@ -158,6 +158,16 @@
 main::ok( !$MATCH, '$MATCH disabled' );
 main::ok( !$POSTMATCH, '$POSTMATCH disabled' );

+
+# Check that both variables change when localized.
+{
+    local $LIST_SEPARATOR = "wibble";
+    ::is $", 'wibble', '$" changes when $LIST_SEPARATOR is localized';
+
+    local $" = 'frooble';
+    ::is $LIST_SEPARATOR, 'frooble';
+}
+
 __END__
